   "title": "Start here",
   "widgets_values": [
    "# MiniMax H3 Talking Head - Batch\n\n768 x 768, 8 steps with the 768p Turbo LoRA. Switch Turbo off for 20 steps of the base model: the best quality, about 2.5x slower.\n\n**Red nodes are the ones you set.** Everything else runs on its own. The stages run left to right, 1 to 7, each with a note underneath.\n\n1. **Load Portrait** - one person facing the camera, face clearly visible.\n2. **Audio From Folder** - put your voiceovers in `ComfyUI/input/batch_audio/` (.wav, .mp3, .flac, .m4a, .aac, .ogg, .opus). Each file becomes its own video, in name order. Upload them with Jupyter (port 8888) or FileBrowser.\n3. **Talking-Head Prompt** - describe the person and background in the portrait.\n4. Run with **batch count 1** to test the first chunk of the first file. Check `output/h3_longform/<name>/chunk_0000.mp4`: lips, face, background.\n5. Run again with a large batch count: roughly the **total seconds of all files / 8**, plus a margin. Each run renders the next unfinished chunk of the next unfinished file. When every file is done the queue is cleared, so extra runs cost nothing.\n6. The final video lands in `output/`, then the queue is cleared.\n\n**Add files later:** drop them in the folder and run again; finished videos are skipped. The same portrait and description are used for every file.\n\nIf the batch count box stops at 100, click Run several times: the queue adds up.\n\nLicence and full instructions: https://github.com/tenitsky/minimax-h3"
   ],
   "color": "#222",
   "bgcolor": "#000"
  },
  {
