   },
   "title": "About stage 1",
   "widgets_values": [
    "## 1. Inputs\n\n**Portrait:** one person facing the camera, face clearly visible, in front of the background you want to keep. It is pinned as the first and last frame of every chunk. Any size; it is center-cropped to the canvas.\n\n**Canvas** (Width x Height). H3's native canvas has a **768 px short edge**, max 768 x 1344:\n\n| Aspect | Width x Height |\n|---|---|\n| 1:1 | 768 x 768 |\n| 3:4 | 768 x 1024 |\n| 9:16 | 768 x 1344 |\n| 16:9 | 1344 x 768 |\n\nDraft uses 544 x 544. Larger canvases need more memory and time."
   ],
   "color": "#222",
   "bgcolor": "#000"
  },
  {
   "id": 4,
   "type": "MarkdownNote",
   "pos": [
    1320,
    930
   ],
   "size": [
    520,
    560
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 3,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
   },
   "title": "About stage 2",
   "widgets_values": [
    "## 2. Describe the shot - this keeps the background steady\n\nH3 pins your portrait only at the **first and last frame** of each chunk. Every frame in between is generated, and the model fills whatever the prompt leaves open: a changing backdrop, a lower-third, a channel logo.\n\n- **subject:** who is on screen and what they wear, as seen in the portrait.\n- **background:** what is behind them, concretely (colour, objects, lighting). Naming it is what holds it in place.\n- **delivery:** how they speak.\n- **extra** (optional): one small, calm action. Keep motion small.\n\nThe fields come filled in for an example portrait: rewrite them for yours. The `subject:` style tags are optional and are removed automatically.\n\nThe node writes MiniMax's exact prompt format for every chunk: a locked-off camera, one person, and no text, logos or graphics.\n\n**Still seeing changes?** Be more specific about the background, lower `max_seconds` on Split to 8, and use a portrait with a plain, evenly lit background."
   ],
   "color": "#222",
   "bgcolor": "#000"
  },
  {
   "id": 5,
   "type": "MarkdownNote",
   "pos": [
    1980,
    590
   ],
   "size": [
    520,
    560
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 4,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
   },
   "title": "About stage 3",
   "widgets_values": [
    "## 3. Chunk plan\n\nH3 renders up to ~15 s at once, so the voiceover is cut into **chunks of up to 10 s**, preferably in pauses. Shorter chunks leave less time for the picture to drift between the pinned portraits.\n\n**Each run renders the next unfinished chunk**, found from the files on disk (`auto_chunk`). There is no counter to reset: a new voiceover starts at chunk 1 in its own folder, and an interrupted render continues where it stopped.\n\nH3 only generates **17k+5 frames** (124, 141 ... 362), so chunk lengths are planned on that grid; the extra pinned frame at each join is dropped, so nothing plays twice.\n\n**motion_carry** (experimental, default off): with 5 or 22 frames, each chunk opens on the previous chunk's last frames instead of the portrait, so head motion continues across the join. Choose it before a render starts; change `name_suffix` when switching it."
   ],
   "color": "#222",
   "bgcolor": "#000"
  },
  {
   "id": 6,
   "type": "MarkdownNote",
   "pos": [
    2640,
    2050
   ],
   "size": [
    520,
    420
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 5,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
   },
   "title": "About stage 4",
   "widgets_values": [
    "## 4. Models + speed - loaded automatically\n\nNothing to set here. Setup downloads every file on first boot.\n\n**Turbo on** (default): the 8-step **768p** Turbo LoRA with its trained video/audio shift of 6/3. **Turbo off**: 20 steps of the base model at its default shift 12/3 - the best quality, about 2.5x slower.\n\n**Attention backend:** Comfy Kitchen INT8 attention, ComfyUI's built-in quantized attention (the same idea as SageAttention). Set it to `pytorch attention` to compare quality.\n\n**Model Sparse Attention** (Sol-Attn) is **bypassed** here to keep this the quality reference. Select it and press Ctrl+B to enable it."
   ],
   "color": "#222",
   "bgcolor": "#000"
  },
  {
   "id": 7,
   "type": "MarkdownNote",
   "pos": [
    3300,
    1210
   ],
   "size": [
    520,
    300
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 6,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
   },
   "title": "About stage 5",
   "widgets_values": [
    "## 5. Portrait + voice guidance\n\n- The portrait is cropped to the canvas and pinned as the **first and last frame** of the chunk (with motion carry, the first frames come from the previous chunk instead).\n- The chunk's slice of your voiceover is pinned at frame 0, so H3 animates the lips to your audio instead of inventing its own speech.\n- The text encoder reads the prompt together with the portraits.\n\nNothing to set here."
   ],
   "color": "#222",
   "bgcolor": "#000"
  },
  {
   "id": 8,
   "type": "MarkdownNote",
   "pos": [
    3960,
    1040
   ],
   "size": [
    520,
    220
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 7,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
   },
   "title": "About stage 6",
   "widgets_values": [
    "## 6. Sampling + decode\n\nFixed seed, Euler sampler and the step count the Turbo LoRA was distilled for. Nothing to set here.\n\nOut of memory? Lower `max_seconds` on Split (stage 3), or use the Draft workflow."
   ],
   "color": "#222",
   "bgcolor": "#000"
  },
  {
   "id": 9,
   "type": "MarkdownNote",
   "pos": [
    4620,
    550
   ],
   "size": [
    520,
    380
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 8,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
   },
   "title": "About stage 7",
   "widgets_values": [
    "## 7. Save + stitch\n\nEach chunk is saved to `output/h3_longform/<name>/chunk_0000.mp4`, ... as it finishes, so you can check one early.\n\nEach file's video is saved as `output/<file name><suffix>.mp4`, stitched with your **original** audio track, not H3's reconstruction.\n\n**Resume:** run again; finished chunks are skipped. **Redo one chunk:** delete its file and run; it is re-rendered and the video re-stitched. **Render a finished video again:** change `name_suffix`, or delete its folder under `output/h3_longform/`."
   ],
   "color": "#222",
   "bgcolor": "#000"
  },
